Z||000006||2xsess||05-10-2001||11:07 AM||||All I've to say is what did these people think about "The Nutty Professor"? Is that insulting too?<P>I'm with you Galen, ppl need to just get over it!||||reg||1
Z||000007||frontal lobe||05-10-2001||12:39 PM||||Actually, yes, I remember seeing on the news when "Nutty Professor" came out that there was the usual "outrage" over the depiction and treatment of obese people.<P>I agree.  Get over it.  If they had a movie that made fun of a character with a receding hairline and gray hair I could somehow manage to still show my face in public without being humiliated. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||DRH||05-10-2001||01:21 PM||||In the words of the Eagles... "Get Over It" from 1994 - Hell Freezes Over. The lyrics describe this trend to a tee...<P>Frontal Lobe, The way I look at it the gray hairs are good. That means their planning on staying with me a while longer.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Galen||05-10-2001||03:49 PM||||Cheever, but you envy my 88 4banger  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe<P>Okey, I'll touch on the rest of that show now, a little bit. They were talking about eminem being homophobic and bashing homosexuals. I was thinking about this earlier, came to the conclusion that most gay people must be heterophobic(sp?). Just because someone dislikes homosexual people does not mean that they are homophobic. In my opinion homophobic means afraid or a fear of homosexual people, however, I did look it up in  <A HREF="http://www.dictionary.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dictionary.com</A>  and it states the meaning is "Aversion to gay or homosexual people or their lifestyle or culture.". In my opinionated meaning, if someone calls me homophobic, they are insulting me. Basicly calling me scared. I admit, things scare me. Homosexual people do not. <P>In Eminems song 'stan' the following lines are stated. to those who know the song you'll know what I am talking about.<P>"PS, We should be together too Said by the character stan.<BR>Eminem responds later in the song with "Whats this sh!t about us meant to be together, that type of sh!t will make me not wanna meet each other".<P>the people(homosexual activists?) said that song is a homophobic song and he bashes homosexuals in it. That was simply funny in my mind, How can that be homophobic? Thats would be a natural reaction for ANY one to have, specially 'famous' people. I do not yet rest my case on opening the eyes of the world to be less sensitive. Am I better than them? or just another activist? I'm a realist, is that bad?<P>sorry for the long somewhat confusing posts. Needed to get it off my head.<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||beer_stud_21||05-10-2001||04:35 PM||||Well I've recently devoloped quite a bit of respect for Eminem.  I've never in my life been into the "rap" sorta music, but I've recently been listening to a few of eminems songs including the before mentioned "stan"  His lryics are definitly colorfull, and a lot of that is needless, but on the other hand that is a big part of why he does it in my opionion.  The more contriversial his songs the more publicity he recieves.  I especially like "who knew" He is drawing attention to a lot of the problems this country has been having over the last 30 yrs. He mentions things I see every day: Things like 12 year old girls wearing makeup, kids with uncles that are 3-4 years older than they are. Kids learing to swear from their bus driver cussin at them.  Kids bein exposed to voilence all the time yet parents only have a hard time with eminems music.  Its hard for me to totally explain his lyrics because I can't type fast enough to keep up with them while i listen to the song, but anybody that wants to can go on napster and download it Eminem "who knew" It really points out a lot of problems and points out how hypicritical we are.  It could really be the theme song for this thread.<P>-Marlin     ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Butter||05-10-2001||05:14 PM||||I was skinny now I'm fat. And I've enjoyed the movies and artist yall been talkin' bout.  I just didn't find anything I needed to get over.  Sounds like people lookin' for trouble.  Hell I just wait for trouble and when it finds me it don't want me no mo.||||reg||12
Z||000012||Taijiguy||05-12-2001||10:19 AM||||I loved the comment about the professional victim thing..I had an encounter with a black guy once who tried to use the race card, and got it jammed firmly in his pooper:<BR>A few years ago I had an altercation with a neighbor over his dog. I confronted him about how inconsiderate it was for him to allow his dog to sit outside and howl all night keeping me and many others awake while he was at work. (he worked night shift someplace) Well, apparently he didn't like being confronted, and when I turned to walk away he sucker punched me from behind. (Guess I didn't sense his <I>chi</I> very well)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> After a brief encounter where he learned I wasn't a victim, I went home called the police and had him arrested just to emphasize my point. (fortunately there were witnesses to his hitting me first)<BR>In court, after his lawyer went through a lengthy line of B/S, he concluded by saying that he felt this whole thing was racially motivated. "Racially motivated?" He slugged <B>me</B>....from <B>behind</B>!<BR>The judge asked me if I had anything to add. I told the story, and concluded by saying that yes, it was possible the whole thing had been racially motivated, but I couldn't for the life of me see what my Scottish heritage could have had to do with it. With the exception of the guy and his lawyer, everyone had a pretty good laugh.<BR>It's true, people take themselves waaaaaay too seriously. It's a fear thing. Life's too short. Lighten up.<BR>~Taiji<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 05-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||johnt671||05-13-2001||02:10 PM||||There are very few people in my life whose opinions of me matter and other than those folks I could care less of others.  I go out of my way to be nice and polite to others and if this is not returned I feel they aren't worthy of any concern from me.||||reg||1
